So I was down in the Gnome King's wine cellar,
getting ready to pick-ax my way to improved luck,
and this cross-aligned unicorn started making a
nuisance of itself in the empty space just outside
the right hand wall.  I quickly whacked it with
Excaliber, and it dropped all the vault's valuable
gems, including the luckstone and the loadstone,
right at my feet.

Somehow this rather takes the zest out of Mines End.
When you've worked so hard to get this far (still
lacking any source of reflection for my lawful
monk), having stuff handed to you on a platter seems
like cheating somehow.

